  "caveats": [
    "The additive structure is imposed because MSRS-2 showed it ranks metals better. A metal-specific slope is therefore not available to the extrapolation.",
    "Three descriptors cannot span five metals; a poor rank correlation is a property of the descriptor table, not of the learner.",
    "Censored rows are dropped (potency 18.4%), so the extrapolation is fitted on the potent side of each metal's cohort.",
    "LOMO evaluates one metal at a time; the five test cohorts differ in size and in ligand chemistry, so the per-metal numbers are not exchangeable."
  ]
